<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44427" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sīpho</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-on</span></b> ; in many MSS. also written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sīfo</span></b> ), ōnis,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίφων</span> (a small pipe).
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A siphon</i> (called also diabetes): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sipho, quem diabeten vocant mechanici,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 10, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">9, 14, 15</span></i>;
			Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fin. 2, 8, 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Q.
				N. 2, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 65, 66, § 166</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">32, 10, 42, §
				124</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 7, 156</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 6,
			310</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A little pipe to suck drinks through</i>, <i>a drinking-tube</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 1, 8 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A kind of fireengine</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 33, 7, 12, § 18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep.
				10, 42, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Isid. 20, 6,
		9</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
